  data: {
    LLM: 'Forehand leads to the first trick. Any card may be led. Players must follow suit if possible; if void, may play any card. With trumps the trick is won by the highest trump; with no trumps, by the highest card of the led suit. There is no obligation to beat or to overtrump. The winner of each trick leads to the next. After 16 tricks, players are scored against their quota for the chosen contract.',
    Player: 'Forehand leads to the first trick. Any card may be led. Players must follow suit if possible; if void, may play any card. With trumps the trick is won by the highest trump; with no trumps, by the highest card of the led suit. There is no obligation to beat or to overtrump. The winner of each trick leads to the next. After 16 tricks, players are scored against their quota for the chosen contract.',
    objective: 'Over 12 deals (each player is forehand 4 times), score the highest cumulative total by managing your tricks relative to your quota.',
    gameplay: 'Forehand leads to the first trick. Any card may be led. Players must follow suit if possible; if void, may play any card. With trumps the trick is won by the highest trump; with no trumps, by the highest card of the led suit. There is no obligation to beat or to overtrump. The winner of each trick leads to the next. After 16 tricks, players are scored against their quota for the chosen contract.',
    keyRules: [
      'Forehand sees 4 face-up cards BEFORE choosing their contract â€” critical information for decision-making.',
      'Forehand picks up the 4 face-up cards and discards 4, keeping 16 for play.',
      'Each contract must be used exactly once per player over 12 deals.',
      '16 tricks per deal (3 players Ã— 16 cards Ã· 3? No â€” 48 cards Ã· 3 = 16 each, so 16 tricks).',
